        "Very thorough spec: every request atom and nearly every operator decision is stated, and every criterion maps to a named test or command. Gaps are stdin behavior, an explicit memory table-name rule, and little proof for the --convert, --stop-after, --alter and --pk interactions. Minor traceability slip: JKEY-36 is assigned to T5 though T2/T3 regenerate the reference file.",
        "Very thorough spec: every operator decision is recorded and each of 38 acceptance criteria has a named test or a command. The gaps are stdin handling and an explicit memory file-stem table-name rule; the extra options (--stop-after, --alter, --convert) are only covered by a general assumption row.. A [tool] placeholder in the tasks file's execution protocol is a leftover but changes no behavior."
